<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<section xml:id="sec-bare-math">
  <title>Quadratics</title>
  <p>
    The graph of $y = x^2$ is a parabola.
  </p>
  <p>
    Its vertex form is
    $$y = a(x - h)^2 + k$$
    where <m>(h, k)</m> is the vertex.
  </p>
  <p>
    The roots are \(x = \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\).
  </p>
  <p>
    The discriminant b^2 - 4ac decides how many real roots there are.
  </p>
</section>
